From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:18:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 067/117] arm64: dts: apple: t8010: describe SPI2 controller

T8010 exposes a SmartIO SPI controller at 0x20a088000 which is used by the
D111 touchscreen, but the common SoC description only contains the
adjacent SPI3 instance. Boards therefore cannot describe an SPI2 child
without duplicating controller resources.

Add the SPI2 register range, interrupt, reference clock and power domain
to the T8010 SoC node, following the existing SPI3 integration. Leave the
controller disabled so each board remains responsible for chip select, DMA
routing and enabling the instance.

This is a normal SoC resource description and requires no SPI-core or
platform-driver special case. The complete series built all DTBs and the
D111 DTB passed schema validation; the resulting controller probed and
carried the live D111 touchscreen traffic. This patch was checked with
checkpatch.pl --strict.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: 025d5b5e8f4833792886a205577fff661451bebb
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010.dtsi
index 0b9a428f1..7224339e8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010.dtsi
@@ -264,6 +264,18 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		spi2: spi@20a088000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t8010-spi", "apple,spi";
+			reg = <0x2 0x0a088000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 216 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&clkref>;
+			power-domains = <&ps_spi2>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <0>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		spi3: spi@20a08c000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t8010-spi", "apple,spi";
 			reg = <0x2 0x0a08c000 0x0 0x4000>;
